<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estim Tuesday 100,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estim Tuesday 100,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts Tuesday were 100,000 head, compared with 100,000 a week ago and 89,000 a year ago.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts sold $1.00-$1.50 higher than the midsession Monday. Trade was moderate on very good demand and light offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    58.50 -59.50	   59.50 -60.50</p>
<p>few			58.00  60.00	   59.00  61.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    57.50 -59.50	   58.00 -60.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    57.50 -59.50	   58.00 -60.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to 2.00 higher.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs   44.00 -45.50	   44.00 -46.50</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   44.00 -46.50	   44.00 -46.50</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    47.00 -48.00	   47.00 -49.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
